.docname {SDK API}
.docauthor {BakingRL}
.include {docs}
.doclang {en}

The SDK package is `@bakingrl/plugin-sdk`. It contains TypeScript contracts,
definition helpers, telemetry fixtures, and small test utilities for BakingRL
plugin packages.

Runtime permissions are enforced by the BakingRL host. The SDK improves typing
and authoring ergonomics, but it is not a security boundary.

## Import Surface

```ts
import {
  SDK_VERSION,
  defineVisual,
  defineComponent,
  defineService,
  defineConnector,
  setting,
  createCleanup,
  createMockVisualContext,
  createMockServiceContext
} from "@bakingrl/plugin-sdk";
```

The root module also re-exports all telemetry names, payload types, fixtures,
and mock event helpers from the telemetry module.

`SDK_VERSION` is the SDK runtime helper version. In this release it is
`0.2.0`.

## JSON Utility Types

`JsonPrimitive` represents `string`, `number`, `boolean`, or `null`.

`JsonValue` represents a JSON-compatible primitive, array, or object.

`CleanupFn` is a function with no arguments and no return value. Mount methods
can return a cleanup function to detach listeners, timers, observers, or DOM
state created by the export.

## Definition Helpers

Definition helpers return the object they receive, but constrain it with the
right SDK type. Use them on every exported module so TypeScript catches missing
or misspelled lifecycle methods.

`definePlugin(definition)`

Types a package-level definition object:

```ts
import { definePlugin } from "@bakingrl/plugin-sdk";

export default definePlugin({
  id: "com.example.scoreboard",
  name: "Scoreboard",
  version: "1.0.0",
  visuals: {
    scoreboard: () => import("./visuals/scoreboard")
  }
});
```

The current generated package format uses `bakingrl.plugin.json` as the source
of truth for exports, so most plugin authors only need the per-capability
helpers below.

`PluginDefinition` fields:

- `id`: package ID.
- `name`: display name.
- `version`: package version.
- `visuals`: optional record of lazy ESM import functions.
- `components`: optional record of lazy ESM import functions.
- `services`: optional record of lazy ESM import functions.
- `connectors`: optional record of lazy ESM import functions.

`defineVisual(visual)`

Types a visual export. Visuals render into a host-owned browser DOM root and
can subscribe to telemetry, load components, call services, and resolve package
assets.

```ts
import { defineVisual, type VisualContext } from "@bakingrl/plugin-sdk";

export default defineVisual({
  mount(context: VisualContext) {
    context.root.textContent = "Waiting for match data";

    return context.bus.subscribe("GoalScored", (event) => {
      context.root.textContent = `${event.Data.Scorer.Name} scored`;
    });
  }
});
```

`defineComponent(component)`

Types a reusable visual component. Components are mounted by visuals through
`context.components.load(ref)` rather than direct package imports.

```ts
import { defineComponent, type ComponentContext } from "@bakingrl/plugin-sdk";

export default defineComponent({
  mount(context: ComponentContext, props: Record<string, unknown>) {
    context.root.textContent = String(props.label ?? "");
  }
});
```

`defineService(service)`

Types a backend service export. Services can subscribe to backend events, write
permitted registry keys, read and write permitted storage URIs, and expose
callable methods.

```ts
import { defineService } from "@bakingrl/plugin-sdk";

let lastGoal: unknown = null;

export default defineService({
  methods: {
    snapshot() {
      return { lastGoal };
    },
    reset() {
      lastGoal = null;
      return { ok: true };
    }
  }
});
```

`defineConnector(connector)`

Types a backend connector export. Connectors receive the service APIs plus
host-mediated HTTP and WebSocket access. Network hosts must be declared in the
manifest permissions.

```ts
import { defineConnector, type ConnectorContext } from "@bakingrl/plugin-sdk";

export default defineConnector({
  async mount(context: ConnectorContext) {
    context.diagnostics.log("connector ready");
  }
});
```

## Lifecycle Contracts

`VisualExport`

- `mount(context)`: required. Called when the visual instance is created.
- `update(context)`: optional. Called when the host updates instance metadata
  or settings without remounting.
- `unmount()`: optional. Called before the visual instance is destroyed.

`mount` can return `void`, `CleanupFn`, `Promise<void>`, or
`Promise<CleanupFn>`.

`ComponentExport`

- `mount(context, props)`: required. Called when a visual mounts the component.
- `update(props)`: optional. Called when the host updates component props.
- `unmount()`: optional. Called before the component instance is destroyed.

`ServiceExport`

- `mount(context)`: optional. Called when the backend service starts.
- `unmount()`: optional. Called before the service stops.
- `methods`: optional object of callable RPC methods.

Each service method receives `(input, context)` and can return a value or a
promise. Inputs and outputs should be JSON-compatible because they cross a
host-mediated RPC boundary.

`ConnectorExport`

- `mount(context)`: optional. Called when the backend connector starts.
- `unmount()`: optional. Called before the connector stops.

Connectors do not define service RPC methods in the current SDK contract. Use a
service export when other plugin code needs callable methods.

## Visual Context

Visuals receive `VisualContext`:

- `root`: the `HTMLElement` owned by this visual instance.
- `package`: package descriptor with `id`, `name`, and `enabled`.
- `exportName`: visual export name from `bakingrl.plugin.json`.
- `item`: layout or page instance metadata.
- `settings`: merged package and item settings.
- `setActive(active)`: informs the host that the visual wants event-layer
  activity enabled or disabled.
- `bus`: telemetry subscription API.
- `registry`: read-only registry API.
- `components`: component loading API.
- `services`: service RPC API.
- `assets`: package asset URL resolver.
- `diagnostics`: structured logging API.

`item` contains:

- `id`, `package_id`, `export_name`, and `name`;
- position fields `x`, `y`, `width`, `height`, and `z_index`;
- state fields `visible`, `locked`, and `opacity`;
- instance `settings`.

Example:

```ts
import { defineVisual, setting, type VisualContext } from "@bakingrl/plugin-sdk";

export default defineVisual({
  mount(context: VisualContext) {
    const accent = setting(context.settings, "accent", "#38bdf8");
    context.root.style.setProperty("--accent", accent);
  },
  update(context) {
    context.root.style.opacity = String(context.item.opacity);
  }
});
```

## Component Context

Components receive `ComponentContext`:

- `root`: the `HTMLElement` owned by this component instance.
- `providerPackageId`: package ID that provides the component.
- `exportName`: component export name from the provider manifest.
- `assets`: provider package asset URL resolver.
- `diagnostics`: structured logging API.

Components should render only inside `root` and should treat `props` as
untrusted input.

## Service Context

Services receive `ServiceContext`:

- `bus`: backend event API with subscribe and emit.
- `registry`: permitted registry read/write API.
- `storage`: permitted text storage API.
- `services`: service RPC API for permitted service imports.
- `settings`: package settings reader.
- `diagnostics`: structured logging API.

Example:

```ts
import { defineService, type ServiceContext } from "@bakingrl/plugin-sdk";

export default defineService({
  mount(context: ServiceContext) {
    return context.bus.subscribe("UpdateState", (event) => {
      context.registry.set("plugin.com.example.scoreboard.state", event.Data);
    });
  }
});
```

## Connector Context

`ConnectorContext` extends `ServiceContext` with host-mediated network APIs:

- `fetch(input, init)`: performs a permitted HTTP request.
- `websocket.connect(url)`: opens a permitted WebSocket connection.

The SDK currently types network values as `unknown` because the host adapter is
the authority for concrete request and socket shapes. Narrow values in your
connector code after checking the host behavior you depend on.

## Runtime APIs

`VisualBus.subscribe(eventName, callback)`

Subscribes to a telemetry or plugin event and returns a cleanup function.

```ts
const off = context.bus.subscribe("ClockUpdatedSeconds", (event) => {
  context.root.textContent = String(event.Data.TimeSeconds);
});
```

For known Rocket League telemetry events, the callback data is typed from
`RlTelemetryPayloadByEvent`. Unknown event names are typed as `unknown`.

`BackendBus.emit(eventName, payload)`

Publishes an event from a backend service. The package manifest must allow the
published event name.

```ts
context.bus.emit("plugin.com.example.scoreboard.ready", { ok: true });
```

`ReadonlyRegistry.get(key)`

Reads a registry value and resolves `null` when the key is absent or not
available to the caller.

```ts
const value = await context.registry.get("plugin.com.example.scoreboard.state");
```

`Registry.get(key)` and `Registry.set(key, value)`

Backend services can synchronously read and write permitted registry values.

```ts
const previous = context.registry.get("plugin.com.example.scoreboard.count");
context.registry.set("plugin.com.example.scoreboard.count", Number(previous ?? 0) + 1);
```

`PluginStorage.readText(uri)` and `PluginStorage.writeText(uri, contents)`

Reads and writes text at permitted storage URIs such as `plugin://self/state.json`.
The current SDK only defines text storage helpers.

```ts
await context.storage.writeText("plugin://self/state.json", JSON.stringify({ ok: true }));
const raw = await context.storage.readText("plugin://self/state.json");
```

`ComponentLoader.load(ref)`

Loads a component through the host and resolves a `ComponentHandle`. References
are package/export strings.

```ts
const component = await context.components.load("com.example.ui/TeamBadge");
const cleanup = await component.mount(context.root, {
  teamName: "Blue",
  color: "#38bdf8"
});
```

`ComponentHandle.mount(root, props)`

Mounts the loaded component into the provided DOM root. It can resolve a cleanup
function.

`ServiceCaller.call(ref, method, input)`

Calls a permitted service method and resolves the method output.

```ts
const snapshot = await context.services.call("com.example.stats/matchStats", "snapshot");
```

`AssetResolver.url(ref)`

Returns a host-safe URL for an asset in the provider package.

```ts
const logoUrl = context.assets.url("assets/logo.png");
```

`SettingsReader.get(key)` and `SettingsReader.all()`

Backend settings access. `get` returns `undefined` when the key is absent.

```ts
const pollMs = context.settings.get<number>("pollMs") ?? 5000;
const settings = context.settings.all();
```

`Diagnostics.log(message, data)`, `Diagnostics.warn(message, data)`, and
`Diagnostics.error(message, data)`

Use diagnostics instead of ad hoc console logging when a context provides it.

```ts
context.diagnostics.warn("missing optional setting", { key: "accent" });
```

## Helper Functions

`setting(settings, key, fallback)`

Reads a value from a plain settings object. It returns `fallback` only when the
stored value is `undefined` or `null`.

```ts
const showBoost = setting(context.settings, "showBoost", true);
```

`createCleanup()`

Creates a cleanup stack with two methods:

- `add(cleanup)`: records function values and returns the original argument.
- `run()`: runs recorded cleanup functions in reverse order.

```ts
import { createCleanup, defineVisual } from "@bakingrl/plugin-sdk";

export default defineVisual({
  mount(context) {
    const cleanup = createCleanup();
    cleanup.add(context.bus.subscribe("GoalScored", () => {}));

    const timer = window.setInterval(() => {}, 1000);
    cleanup.add(() => window.clearInterval(timer));

    return cleanup.run;
  }
});
```

`createMockVisualContext(partial)`

Builds a browser-only mock visual context for local tests. Pass a partial
context to override any default value.

```ts
import { createMockVisualContext } from "@bakingrl/plugin-sdk";
import visual from "../src/visuals/scoreboard";

const context = createMockVisualContext({
  settings: { accent: "#38bdf8" }
});

await visual.mount(context);
```

The mock creates a `div` root, a package descriptor, a layout item, no-op
host APIs, and console-backed diagnostics.

`createMockServiceContext(partial)`

Builds a backend service context for tests. It includes an in-memory registry,
no-op bus, no-op storage, no-op service caller, empty settings, and
console-backed diagnostics.

```ts
import { createMockServiceContext } from "@bakingrl/plugin-sdk";
import service from "../src/services/match-stats";

const context = createMockServiceContext();
await service.mount?.(context);
```

## Reference Strings

The SDK does not parse reference strings. The host owns lookup and permission
checks. Use these forms consistently:

- `package-id/exportName` for component and service references.
- `plugin.<package-id>.*` for package-owned bus events and registry keys.
- `plugin://self/...` for package-owned storage paths.

Declare imports and permissions in `bakingrl.plugin.json` so the host can
authorize those references at runtime.
